course: dictionary
lesson: 7719
title: Publicly: in front of people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Publicly means in front of other people, openly, not in private. «She publicly thanked her teacher» means she said thank you where everyone could hear, not quietly in a corner. The clue is the word thanked: someone who thanks another person in public wants the whole room to hear it.
explain: The word has a second meaning, linked to the government and the public. «Publicly funded schools» are paid for by the government with public money, so everyone can use them. Publicly owned means owned by the state, not by one private person or company.
explain: Public ends in -ic, and many words ending in -ic add -ally (basic, basically), so you might expect publically. But publicly is the exception, so spell it publicly. Check the meaning by swapping in a simple phrase: in front of people fits, so publicly is the right word.
fact: Publicly means in front of other people, openly, not in private.
fact: «Publicly» also means by or for the government or the public, as in «publicly funded».
fact: Public ends in -ic, so you might expect -ally, but the spelling is «publicly».
fact: «Publicly available» means anyone can see or use it.
fact: Photos posted publicly can be collected and used to make fakes, so you may ask family not to post yours.
exercise: «She publicly thanked her teacher.» What does publicly mean here? | *In front of other people | Very late at night | Only with her best friend | In a quiet, private place
exercise: «Publicly funded schools» are paid for by whom? | *The government, using public money from taxes | Parents only | The children's sports clubs | Their owners in private
exercise: Which spelling is correct for the adverb from public? | publically | publickly | *publicly | publikly
test: Why is publicly the exception to the -ic rule? | Because it ends in -ally | *Because public ends in -ic, but the adverb is spelled publicly, not publically | Because it is a noun | Because it means in private
test: Ruby will announce the winner ___ at assembly, so everyone hears. | secretly | *publicly | quietly | in private
exam: «Photos posted publicly» means posted where? | *Where anyone can see them | Only to the police | In a locked box | In a diary
